    sum: "Kraków's fantasy Christmas cribs stacking St Mary's spires and Wawel towers in coloured foil — an annual competition that turned street cribs into national art.",
    desc: "Kraków szopki are miniature castles of Christmas: slender Gothic spires modelled on St Mary's Basilica, Wawel's courtyard arcade, domes and clock tiers, all sheathed in shiny coloured foil and populated by puppet carollers, folk devils, Turks and dragons. Born in the 19th century as portable street cribs for carollers earning coins, they were rescued from decline when an annual competition was launched in 1937, a tradition now run by the Historical Museum of Kraków. Building is a family craft transmitted across generations, with symmetry, spire count and moving figures judged each December on the Main Square. UNESCO inscribed the tradition in 2018. The aesthetic is gleaming, vertical, symmetric and gleefully over-stuffed — folklore and cathedral condensed into a shoebox skyline.",
