    sum: "Valencia's March inferno of art — towering satirical ninot sculptures that joke through the streets for days, then burn whole in la Cremà.",
    desc: "Falles are enormous figurative sculptures — ninots — built by neighbourhood casal communities from wood, papier-mâché and polystyrene, satirising politicians and fads with a carpenter's cruel accuracy, raised on street corners for the festival of St Joseph. For five days the city runs on gunpowder mascletà barrages, street bands and lights, until la Cremà on 19 March ignites every falla at once, streets turning to a canyon of controlled fire. Each year one ninot is pardoned by public vote — the ninot indultat — and enters the Falles Museum with decades of saved figures. UNESCO inscribed the festival in 2016, and artists' guilds train fallero sculptors through apprenticeships. The aesthetic is saturated pop-baroque: neon spray, flesh-pink modelling, gutter caricature and firelight.",
